ariance, blockers, decisions, and agentic AI provenance when applicable. Use when reporting project status to stakeholders.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.agents/skills/project-status-report/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>prompt-meta</name>\n    <description>Prompt engineering on this repo: extract a reusable prompt from a successful interaction, distill it to token-efficient form, verify the distilled version preserved essential instructions. Trigger for capture/distill/verify prompt work.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.agents/skills/prompt-meta/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>pwa-accessibility-review</name>\n    <description>4-domain heuristic review of PWAs targeting non-technical merchants on entry-level devices with volatile connectivity. Use when reviewing PWAs for non-technical low-end users.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.agents/skills/pwa-accessibility-review/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>renew</name>\n    <description>Compiled alias of the resume prior work mode of the session skill. Hidden from model invocation; invocable via /skill:renew; serves the legacy site URL with full compiled content.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.agents/skills/renew/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>research-codebase</name>\n    <description>Structured investigation of unfamiliar codebases. Use when onboarding to an unfamiliar codebase.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.agents/skills/research-codebase/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>research-review</name>\n    <description>Iterative review of research documents using Rule of 5. Use only when iteratively reviewing research documents.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.agents/skills/research-review/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>resonant-refactor</name>\n    <description>Safe, human-approved refactoring workflow with